1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,800
On 17 July 2014, a Boeing 777
left Amsterdam for Kuala Lumpur.

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,800
Flight MH17.

3
00:00:09,165 --> 00:00:13,405
Less than three hours later, over eastern
Ukraine, it broke apart in the sky.

4
00:00:13,635 --> 00:00:17,205
Two hundred and ninety-eight people died.

5
00:00:18,439 --> 00:00:21,219
Twelve years later,
while we were preparing this video,

6
00:00:21,299 --> 00:00:24,099
a clip from Russian radio
went round the internet.

7
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:27,979
In it, a retired Russian colonel
appeared to say:

8
00:00:28,079 --> 00:00:30,699
"A Russian officer shot it down, yes."

9
00:00:31,115 --> 00:00:34,775
It looked like the admission
investigators had been waiting for.

10
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:37,630
We'll come back to what he actually said.

11
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:40,830
Because to judge a confession,
you first need to know

12
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:43,110
what the evidence says without it.

13
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:45,900
So who really shot down MH17?

14
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:49,360
And how can anyone know,
when the crime scene was in a war zone,

15
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,560
and the truth itself became a weapon?

16
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,900
The first question was the simplest one.

17
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:58,880
What destroyed the aircraft?

18
00:00:59,766 --> 00:01:03,106
The Dutch Safety Board answered it
in October 2015.

19
00:01:03,926 --> 00:01:07,306
A warhead exploded just above
and to the left of the cockpit.

20
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:11,360
It sprayed the front of the plane
with hundreds of metal fragments.

21
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,900
The three people in the cockpit
were killed instantly.

22
00:01:15,706 --> 00:01:18,546
Some of those fragments
had an unusual shape.

23
00:01:19,026 --> 00:01:20,226
A bow tie.

24
00:01:20,617 --> 00:01:23,017
That shape comes from one kind of warhead:

25
00:01:23,197 --> 00:01:27,017
the one carried by the Buk,
a Soviet-designed surface-to-air missile.

26
00:01:27,817 --> 00:01:32,597
Investigators found those fragments in the
wreckage, and in the body of the captain.

27
00:01:33,537 --> 00:01:35,097
And they rebuilt the front of the plane

28
00:01:35,327 --> 00:01:38,757
from recovered pieces,
to check that the damage fitted.

29
00:01:39,278 --> 00:01:41,898
So within fifteen months,
the weapon was known.

30
00:01:41,998 --> 00:01:44,438
But a weapon is not a person.

31
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,978
It doesn't tell you who fired it.

32
00:01:47,485 --> 00:01:50,965
By the way, if you like videos
like this, consider subscribing.

33
00:01:51,585 --> 00:01:53,205
It really helps the channel.

34
00:01:55,575 --> 00:01:58,335
For the people on board,
it came without warning.

35
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,120
A blast, a sudden loss of pressure,

36
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,800
violent wind and cold,
and an aircraft coming apart.

37
00:02:05,559 --> 00:02:08,339
The fall lasted
a minute to a minute and a half.

38
00:02:08,719 --> 00:02:11,359
Whether anyone stayed
aware for part of it,

39
00:02:11,439 --> 00:02:14,799
the investigators could neither confirm
nor rule out.

40
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:18,605
What they did judge likely
is that people were barely able

41
00:02:18,835 --> 00:02:20,565
to understand what was happening.

42
00:02:21,019 --> 00:02:22,839
That is why precision matters here.

43
00:02:23,069 --> 00:02:28,119
Two hundred and ninety-eight people, and
their families, are owed the right answer.

44
00:02:30,809 --> 00:02:32,709
Then there was the crime scene.

45
00:02:33,401 --> 00:02:36,441
The plane came down near Hrabove,
in territory held

46
00:02:36,671 --> 00:02:39,861
by Russian-backed separatists,
in the middle of a war.

47
00:02:40,431 --> 00:02:43,351
International monitors
arrived the next day.

48
00:02:43,971 --> 00:02:46,331
Armed men decided where they could go.

49
00:02:46,971 --> 00:02:49,131
The bodies were taken away by train.

50
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:52,891
The flight recorders
were handed over four days later.

51
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:56,240
Parts of the wreckage
were moved or cut up.

52
00:02:56,820 --> 00:03:00,500
Dutch investigators could not search
the site properly for months.

53
00:03:01,226 --> 00:03:02,846
So here is the problem.

54
00:03:03,626 --> 00:03:06,686
If the people holding the crime scene
are part of the conflict,

55
00:03:06,766 --> 00:03:08,946
how do you trust anything found there?

56
00:03:09,452 --> 00:03:12,452
The answer is that you don't
have to rely on it alone.

57
00:03:12,792 --> 00:03:16,392
Because a lot of the evidence
was never lying in that field.

58
00:03:18,902 --> 00:03:22,622
Some of it was posted online
within about an hour of the crash.

59
00:03:23,371 --> 00:03:26,811
A page on VKontakte,
Russia's version of Facebook,

60
00:03:26,891 --> 00:03:29,111
called "Dispatches from Strelkov",

61
00:03:29,391 --> 00:03:32,491
announced that an An-26
had been shot down near Torez.

62
00:03:33,515 --> 00:03:36,395
Strelkov was the field name
of Igor Girkin,

63
00:03:36,475 --> 00:03:38,635
the separatists' military commander.

64
00:03:40,171 --> 00:03:42,531
An An-26 is a military transport plane.

65
00:03:42,991 --> 00:03:45,071
The post added: "We warned them.

66
00:03:45,151 --> 00:03:46,691
Do not fly in our sky."

67
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:51,647
When it became clear that the plane
was a passenger jet, the post disappeared.

68
00:03:52,336 --> 00:03:53,836
So what does that prove?

69
00:03:54,316 --> 00:03:56,036
Not that Girkin wrote it.

70
00:03:56,636 --> 00:04:00,476
The page was run by his supporters,
and he has denied writing it.

71
00:04:01,012 --> 00:04:03,252
Not who fired the missile, either.

72
00:04:03,703 --> 00:04:06,303
What it does show
is that so soon after the crash,

73
00:04:06,523 --> 00:04:07,983
someone on the separatist side

74
00:04:08,213 --> 00:04:10,823
was claiming a shoot-down,
at that place and that time,

75
00:04:11,053 --> 00:04:13,743
of what they took for a military plane.

76
00:04:16,253 --> 00:04:20,093
Phone calls intercepted later that day
point the same way.

77
00:04:20,793 --> 00:04:24,033
Separatist fighters
realised the plane had been civilian.

78
00:04:24,735 --> 00:04:29,675
Those calls came from Ukraine's security
service, which is one side of the war.

79
00:04:30,275 --> 00:04:33,715
So the investigators had them checked
for signs of editing.

80
00:04:35,033 --> 00:04:36,773
Then there were the photographs.

81
00:04:37,625 --> 00:04:40,665
Earlier that day, people in Donetsk,
Torez and Snizhne

82
00:04:40,745 --> 00:04:45,465
photographed and filmed a Buk launcher,
mostly on a low loader, moving east.

83
00:04:46,147 --> 00:04:48,587
A single photo proves very little.

84
00:04:49,227 --> 00:04:52,527
It can be misdated, staged,
or taken somewhere else.

85
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,500
So each one was checked.

86
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,020
Shadows against the time of day.

87
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,600
Buildings against satellite images.

88
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:02,280
Posts against when they first appeared.

89
00:05:02,999 --> 00:05:04,879
The next morning, a video from Luhansk

90
00:05:05,109 --> 00:05:07,739
showed the same kind of launcher
heading for Russia,

91
00:05:08,019 --> 00:05:09,559
with one missile missing.

92
00:05:10,042 --> 00:05:11,862
And it wasn't just any launcher.

93
00:05:12,602 --> 00:05:14,622
Marks on its side
matched a vehicle photographed

94
00:05:14,852 --> 00:05:17,262
weeks earlier in a Russian army convoy.

95
00:05:18,055 --> 00:05:22,155
In 2018, the international
criminal investigation,

96
00:05:22,695 --> 00:05:24,195
the Joint Investigation Team,

97
00:05:24,425 --> 00:05:26,695
concluded that the launcher
came from Russia's

98
00:05:26,925 --> 00:05:31,495
fifty-third Anti-Aircraft Missile Brigade,
based in Kursk.

99
00:05:31,889 --> 00:05:34,169
No single piece proves the case.

100
00:05:34,809 --> 00:05:36,809
What matters is how the photographs,

101
00:05:36,909 --> 00:05:39,409
recordings and physical evidence
fit together,

102
00:05:39,489 --> 00:05:42,629
and whether independent checks
support the same conclusion.

103
00:05:45,489 --> 00:05:49,509
Russia offered other explanations.
Several of them.

104
00:05:49,931 --> 00:05:53,171
In July 2014, the Russian Defence Ministry

105
00:05:53,401 --> 00:05:58,071
pointed to a Ukrainian Su-25 warplane
flying near the airliner.

106
00:05:58,859 --> 00:06:02,899
In 2015, the Buk's Russian maker
agreed that it was a Buk,

107
00:06:02,979 --> 00:06:07,059
but said it was an older missile,
fired from a village held by Ukraine.

108
00:06:07,873 --> 00:06:11,973
In 2016, the ministry released
new radar data.

109
00:06:12,693 --> 00:06:16,873
This time, there was no warplane
near MH17 at all.

110
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:23,440
In 2018, it produced a serial number, and
said the missile had belonged to Ukraine.

111
00:06:24,195 --> 00:06:25,935
Here we need to be careful.

112
00:06:26,475 --> 00:06:28,755
Changing stories don't prove guilt.

113
00:06:29,195 --> 00:06:31,975
People who are innocent
can get things wrong, too.

114
00:06:32,393 --> 00:06:36,413
What the changing stories did, in
practice, was offer a choice of answers.

115
00:06:37,413 --> 00:06:41,853
And when there are so many answers, it's
easy to feel there's no answer at all.

116
00:06:42,411 --> 00:06:45,271
The investigators examined
the Russian claims.

117
00:06:46,051 --> 00:06:47,911
None of them changed the conclusion.

118
00:06:50,621 --> 00:06:52,461
Which brings us back to that colonel.

119
00:06:53,469 --> 00:06:56,082
His name is Viktor Baranets.

120
00:06:56,289 --> 00:06:59,029
Once a spokesman
for a Russian defence minister,

121
00:06:59,109 --> 00:07:03,449
now a military commentator
for the newspaper Komsomolskaya Pravda.

122
00:07:03,935 --> 00:07:06,895
For years, he had dismissed
the case against Russia.

123
00:07:07,437 --> 00:07:12,217
Then, on the paper's radio station
in September 2026, he said:

124
00:07:12,537 --> 00:07:17,117
"A Russian officer shot it down, yes,
because that pest barged into our sky."

125
00:07:17,773 --> 00:07:20,033
A few weeks later, the clip went viral.

126
00:07:20,693 --> 00:07:22,273
It looked like the missing piece.

127
00:07:22,853 --> 00:07:26,073
It even echoed the Strelkov post:
"our sky".

128
00:07:26,553 --> 00:07:29,313
So let's check it the way
we checked everything else.

129
00:07:30,128 --> 00:07:33,648
In the same answer, he said
"Soviet officers" did it.

130
00:07:34,108 --> 00:07:37,208
He said the plane had been warned
by radio, by manoeuvres,

131
00:07:37,438 --> 00:07:40,008
and by tracer fire across its nose.

132
00:07:40,743 --> 00:07:43,103
None of that happened to MH17.

133
00:07:43,863 --> 00:07:45,543
No fighter chased it.

134
00:07:45,983 --> 00:07:48,183
It was hit by a missile from the ground.

135
00:07:48,729 --> 00:07:53,069
But it matches another shootdown,
as Moscow described it at the time.

136
00:07:53,446 --> 00:07:57,206
On 1 September 1983,
a Soviet fighter shot down

137
00:07:57,436 --> 00:08:02,716
Korean Air Lines Flight 007,
which had strayed into Soviet airspace.

138
00:08:02,946 --> 00:08:06,106
Two hundred and sixty-nine people died.

139
00:08:06,406 --> 00:08:07,846
There, "our sky" makes sense.

140
00:08:08,076 --> 00:08:11,846
Baranets almost certainly
mixed up two tragedies.

141
00:08:12,891 --> 00:08:14,471
So it isn't a confession.

142
00:08:15,011 --> 00:08:16,891
Not one we can honestly use.

143
00:08:17,597 --> 00:08:19,757
And this is the uncomfortable part.

144
00:08:19,997 --> 00:08:21,657
We wanted it to be true.

145
00:08:22,217 --> 00:08:24,597
It fitted what the evidence already says.

146
00:08:25,049 --> 00:08:27,749
That is exactly when
you have to check hardest.

147
00:08:28,629 --> 00:08:33,309
A claim that confirms what you believe
gets the same test as one that denies it.

148
00:08:34,008 --> 00:08:35,808
And the case doesn't need him.

149
00:08:38,568 --> 00:08:40,608
So what has actually been proven?

150
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:46,637
In November 2022, a Dutch court convicted
three men for their part in the downing.

151
00:08:46,837 --> 00:08:51,387
Igor Girkin, Sergei Dubinsky
and Leonid Kharchenko.

152
00:08:51,737 --> 00:08:54,077
Life sentences, in their absence.

153
00:08:54,935 --> 00:08:59,815
A fourth man, Oleg Pulatov,
was acquitted. That matters, too.

154
00:09:00,295 --> 00:09:02,135
The court weighed each man separately.

155
00:09:02,949 --> 00:09:07,049
In 2023, the investigators
reported "strong indications"

156
00:09:07,279 --> 00:09:11,769
that the decision to supply the Buk
was taken by President Putin.

157
00:09:12,517 --> 00:09:14,157
Strong indications are not proof.

158
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:18,557
And supplying a weapon
is not ordering it to be fired.

159
00:09:19,237 --> 00:09:23,177
The investigators could not establish
who ordered the missile to be launched.

160
00:09:23,703 --> 00:09:27,003
The crew were never identified
well enough to be charged.

161
00:09:27,403 --> 00:09:30,323
Most likely,
they took it for a military plane.

162
00:09:31,054 --> 00:09:33,274
The investigation was suspended.

163
00:09:34,054 --> 00:09:37,254
In the investigators' words,
it had reached its limits.

164
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:43,200
In 2025, two international bodies,
the UN's civil aviation council

165
00:09:43,430 --> 00:09:47,340
and the European Court of Human Rights,
found Russia responsible.

166
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:52,870
And one more failure belongs on the list.

167
00:09:53,601 --> 00:09:57,321
Ukraine had closed its eastern airspace
up to thirty-two thousand feet.

168
00:09:57,551 --> 00:10:02,338
MH17 was flying at thirty-three thousand.

169
00:10:02,637 --> 00:10:05,617
The Safety Board found
that the flight broke no rules,

170
00:10:05,997 --> 00:10:09,357
but that Ukraine had reason
to close the airspace completely,

171
00:10:09,617 --> 00:10:12,237
and that nobody had properly
weighed the risk.

172
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:14,560
That doesn't excuse the missile.

173
00:10:15,220 --> 00:10:17,960
Several failures can sit
inside one tragedy.

174
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,360
So, who really shot down MH17?

175
00:10:24,608 --> 00:10:26,428
A Buk missile,
from a Russian army launcher,

176
00:10:26,658 --> 00:10:29,208
fired from separatist-held ground.

177
00:10:29,888 --> 00:10:31,488
Three men convicted.

178
00:10:32,228 --> 00:10:34,748
And the hand that fired it,
still without a name.

179
00:10:35,847 --> 00:10:37,587
Gaps like that shouldn't be hidden.

180
00:10:37,667 --> 00:10:40,587
But they don't mean
that nothing can be known.

181
00:10:41,078 --> 00:10:43,038
None of this rests on a confession.

182
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:47,618
It rests on pieces of evidence
that were checked, and still fit together.

183
00:10:48,365 --> 00:10:50,905
The truth isn't the claim
that sounds right.

184
00:10:51,185 --> 00:10:53,895
It's the one still standing
after we check it.
